cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PySNT in your work, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "PySNT: Python interface for SNT"
abstract: >-
  PySNT is a Python interface for SNT, the open-source framework for
  quantification of neuronal anatomy. It brings SNT's tracing, analysis and
  visualization capabilities to Jupyter notebooks and NumPy/pandas-based
  pipelines, and ships with Computational Neuroanatomy: A Hands-on Curriculum
  in Python.
authors:
  - family-names: Ferreira
    given-names: Tiago A.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6866-1540"
    affiliation: "Janelia Research Campus, Howard Hughes Medical Institute"
  - name: "PySNT contributors"
  - name: "SNT contributors"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/morphonets/pysnt"
repository-artifact: "https://pypi.org/project/pysnt/"
url: "https://pysnt.readthedocs.io"
keywords:
  - neuroanatomy
  - neuronal morphology
  - reconstruction
  - SNT
  - Python
  - Fiji
  - ImageJ
